<%#
  The page body.

  TWO FORMS, ON PURPOSE.

  1. MATERIALIZED (`layout_erb` present) -- the page layout has been converted
     from its ACIA tree into static markup by AciaToHerb, and what arrives here
     is real, readable structure: a <main>, the scope trail, the title, the
     five-track board PanelFrame. Everything below the cut is an ACIA render
     reference filled from `slots`. This is the form a Rails 8 developer can
     open, read, and edit.

  2. GENERATED (`layout_erb` absent) -- the whole document is still one blob of
     renderer output. Correct while a page is being discovered; opaque once it
     has a shape worth designing. Moving a page from 2 to 1 is the JIT ->
     fixed-form step, and it is a one-way trip.

  `body` is never re-escaped in either form: it is generated markup from
  Profile9::Renderer, whose node cids are derived from the whole-document
  digest. Re-rendering any part of it in isolation would mint different cids.
%>
<% if defined?(layout_erb) && layout_erb %>
  <%= render inline: layout_erb, locals: { acia: AppOrientedTranslation::SlotBinding.new(slots) } %>
<% else %>
  <%= body.to_s.html_safe %>
<% end %>
